        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int CharProps::width</definition>
        <argsstring>() const noexcept</argsstring>
        <name>width</name>
        <qualifiedname>CharProps::width</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Returns the terminal display width of this character. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Computes the monospace cell width for terminal display. This follows the Unicode Width property (EAW - East Asian Width) where wide characters (East Asian Fullwidth, Wide) have width 2, and most other printable characters have width 1.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>Character width: typically 0 (combining), 1 (regular), or 2 (wide). Negative values may occur for specific combining marks.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Example</title><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">CharProps<sp/>props<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="_char_props_8h_1a7bdc2c8b0aa8edbd7dad4d7d4fe2c1c9" kindref="member">charPropsFor</ref>(</highlight><highlight class="charliteral">&apos;A&apos;</highlight><highlight class="normal">);<sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>width()<sp/>returns<sp/>1</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">CharProps<sp/>props<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="_char_props_8h_1a7bdc2c8b0aa8edbd7dad4d7d4fe2c1c9" kindref="member">charPropsFor</ref>(0x4E00);<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>CJK<sp/>char,<sp/>width()<sp/>returns<sp/>2</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">CharProps<sp/>props<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="_char_props_8h_1a7bdc2c8b0aa8edbd7dad4d7d4fe2c1c9" kindref="member">charPropsFor</ref>(0x0301);<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>combining<sp/>accent,<sp/>width()<sp/>returns<sp/>0</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
